endly as well  this unit has just come out  i've only sold two in two weeks but i  think it will establish itself on the  market  later it will pick up pick up the market  a strategy meeting at godrej marcus  vubia from the german agency for  international cooperation the giz  explains what's required to get a german  eco label a good selling point on the  indian market  in principle this product actually would  also  help the european market to reduce  greenhouse gas emissions  we would like to go into other  international markets obviously  but establish ourselves establish the  technology well  make sure that all the safety  requirements are taken care of then  obviously go forward  in neighboring countries it will  probably be relatively  easy to get established but if they want  to break into the european market  they'll have to fulfill slightly higher  standards  but first their target is the indian  market  the chowdhurys are proud owners of one  of the 1000 odd climate friendly units  sold  so far the installers have been  specially trained by godrej  to make sure not an iota of flammable  propane  can escape  finally the long-awaited moment arrives  and shashikan chowdhury thinks it's just  cool the environment  is also a concern in southern moldova  there the lower proofed floodplain is  home to such rich biodiversity  that it prompted the creation of a  natural park  but then a railway was constructed  through the region the promise was to  promote economic development  but the local flora and fauna are  suffering what's more  locals say they haven't benefited from  the new infrastructure either  lucia thought from trm moldova has that  story  the lower fruit is a scientific reserve  located in the south of the republic of  moldova  many species of migratory birds come  here to breed  the reserve was created to protect the  flora and fauna of the lakes and swamps  around the river fruit  in 2007 a railway was built in this area  to transport goods to the 