e trying to expand your  business amid that turmoil  waheed al-mala from emerging stars tv  introduces us to a young entrepreneur  who is doing  just that and business is booming  let's meet the man who's bringing fresh  bread to cairo  you can see smell even you can hear the  crust  happening in front of you in the oven so  tbs is all about  freshness this could definitely be  called a fresh idea  opening a chain of shops offering fresh  oven-baked bread  a new concept in egypt we visit tbs  the bakery shop and meet one of the  founders  basel mashua he tells us about the  company  and the concept they introduced we have  the  so fresh it's baked in front of you  concept so this is what makes  tbs have a competitive edge versus any  bakery in the market and we simply  thought about this  concept to fill a gap in the market we  were exposed to the  international market whenever we travel  we find good bakeries good smell  walking down the street so we thought  why not  have such a concept in egypt and this is  where it all came from  three young entrepreneurs started the  bakery shop in 2008  none of them knew anything about baking  bread but they were convinced the  egyptian market was ready for freshly  baked products  in the beginning it was a sideline next  to their day jobs  this was pretty hectic because i had to  go and to my working hours from nine to  five  and then i had to manage everything that  had to do with tbs  afterwards so it was a very hectic but i  think this was the safest bet  it was too much risk to drop your  current  job just to for a dream right  the tbs bakery shop is the flagship of  the company  however in order to grow the business  they started offering a wider range of  services  well currently the the company name is  delicious bakery it has  three revenue streams one is tbs the  premium brand  with eight shops and then we have the  shop and shop model under the delicious  bakery name  which is in supermarkets it's seven  shops and then we have the b2b line  which we cater to all the cafes and  restaurants  in each but growing the business also  brings challenges  especially if you want to maintain  quality standards in all the shops  the most difficult thing is the  consistency because the consistency is  the name of the game in our  industry the more we grow and we more  the more we open outlets it gets  more difficult to maintain the the  quality and the  consistency of the product  well first of all uh centralizing the  production was one of the  ways to to to to control this  consistency problem  uh now we have uh  like production manuals where where  where the new employees get  like a month or two months training to  to to to to get trained on exactly the  the shape of the  bread where we want for example if you  can if you can see this low for this  loaf  when you visit any of the tbs outlets  you'll find the the loaf looking exactly  the same because  this is what we want we we're a chain  we're getting bigger  so whenever there's a customer going to  any of our tbs outlets  he has to find the exact same product  currently tbs has eight shops throughout  egypt  managing this is time consuming but  basel mature makes sure he's got enough  time available for his family if  the entrepreneur doesn't see his kids  then it's his problem  because i think you always have to  manage your time to  balance between your work and and your  kids  because what good will it make if you're  making money without  knowing your kids quite well so i guess  i enjoy  my kid every day  right i think we are the new generation  especially after the revolution we are  the generation that  i think would make a difference in in  the next years to come  we really depend on ourselves to make  this country head for a better future a  brighter future  so of course i i think we are the  generation to come  and it's up to us to shape the future of  this country  basel also makes sure he has time for  sports  he used to 