 for  professional portraits are dwindling  in the past there were many freelance  photographers here  at that time photographers could make  enough money  to even buy a house in hanoi  these days people have their own cameras  they're light and easy to use  the digital photography revolution has  made hanoi's freelance photographers  almost obsolete  i have a smartphone and a digital camera  so it's easy and convenient to take  pictures of my friends and family  hiring a photographer is very time  consuming because you have to wait for  them to print the photos  digital photography has allowed people  to gain better knowledge of the craft  and help them develop more discerning  tastes  a freelance photographer can't keep up  with us  and besides the quality of freelance  photographers varies quite a bit  has spent around 20 years taking photos  at honkem lake  he used to take hundreds of pictures for  customers now he's lucky if he gets a  dozen orders  he also runs a photography club with  about 25 members  but there used to be twice as many  we advise younger photographers to see  freelance photography only as a way of  making a bit of extra money  on top of a full-time job  most don't know what to do  with so many amateur photographers  around these days hanoi's freelance  street photographers fear they will soon  be a thing of the past  that's all for this edition of world  stories from all of us here in berlin  and our partner stations around the  world thanks for tuning in  to watch this episode and others head to  our website the address there  d w dot d e world stories before we go  check out this week's picks of the world  enjoy and see you next time  so  you
 

